check: F1 — start-services.sh gates on the 11 Kafka topics existing, not on the broker port answering
==========================

Reproduces the clean-machine first-five-minutes command EXACTLY, from a
'docker compose down -v' (volumes removed), with no pause between the two
halves:

    docker compose -f demo/docker-compose.yml up -d && \
    DEMO_SKIP_BUILD=1 demo/scripts/start-services.sh

'up -d' returns while kafka-init is still running, so the broker has bound
its port but the topics do not exist yet. Before the fix the JVMs started
into that window and failed with UNKNOWN_TOPIC_OR_PARTITION (auto-create is
off). The [demo] timestamps below show the gate holding until they exist.

