=== CORROBORATION: kafka-init was still working during that 11s wait ===
$ docker compose logs --timestamps kafka-init
kafka-init-1  | 2026-08-04T08:55:50.973996970Z Creating Kafka topics...
kafka-init-1  | 2026-08-04T08:56:02.265336128Z All Kafka topics created successfully.

$ docker compose ps -a kafka-init  (exited 0 => topic creation finished)
maestro-demo-kafka-init-1	exited	Exited (0) 19 seconds ago

Timeline: the gate began waiting at 10:55:51 and cleared at 10:56:02.
kafka-init's own 'All Kafka topics created successfully.' falls inside that
window, so the 11s was a genuine wait on missing topics, not a fixed sleep.

=== final topic count on the broker ===
12
(12 = the 11 required topics + Kafka's internal __consumer_offsets; the gate
 checks the required set is a SUBSET of what exists, so extras are fine.)

=== F4 NEGATIVE TEST: ports are checked BEFORE anything starts ===
Services are already running, so a second invocation must refuse all four
ports up front and start no JVM. Before the fix this failed inside
start_jvm, one at a time, leaving earlier JVMs orphaned.

